      "content": "stop with the \"mischievous goblin\" stuff please. i'm trying to figure out if i can fix this myself or if i need to pay a shop. if the tensioner is the problem, do i just replace the tensioner or does that affect the belt too? and how do i actually check if the idler pulley is worn out without taking the whole engine apart?",
